Z||000000||fierospeeder||10-01-2001||02:46 PM||||I have a 12month 12,000 warranty on my Tbird turbo on the transmission rebuild i had done on 2/../2000.   This is by murphys trans.  I had brought my trans there about 3-4 times, about 3 times for rebuilds paying about 900 dollars, not including hard parts.  Notice i brought it there 3 times and i always had to bring it back due to bad rebuilds.<P><BR>My car was slipping when it was cold.  And after it would warm up, reverse would slip and eventually if the trans was hot enough, reverse acted like neutral.<P>I brought the trans in to the guy.  He looked at it, and said it needs a new tv cable.  The only thing he had done was add another zip tie to hold the cable tighter to the throttle body bracket.  My girlfriend was present when i pick it up and said,  Ya, it needs a new tv cable, and if you want you can get another one and bring it in.  I asked can i put it on, he said ya, and we can adjust it for you.  He didn't give any receipt to me.  <P>So i didn't drive the car for est. 4 months.  I couldn't afford the plate sticker, because of my G/F, or the TV cable.  I got another TV cable from the junk yard, it is in perfect condition.  And installed it myself, about a month ago.  Drove the car once.  <P>Once i got my new sticker, i brought my car in for them to fix my car, overdrive and 3 is gone when the car warms up, and reverse still doesn't work.<P>So i called the guy today, and i asked if you guys worked on it.  He said no.  He wont be able to do anything because i tempered with the car.  "owner", i told him i had my trans rebuilt with you guys 3 times and i always had probs, once i got stuck on the side of the road.  He wont fix it because he doesn't know for a fact i didn't drive the car and because i changed the tv cable on my own.<P>My g/f called up also and complained.  No good, he said yada yada i know sh(t about cars.  And that i burnt the trans up because the tv cable wasn't adjusted propery.  BUT reverse didn't work when i first brought the car in.<P>What are my options now.  Yes my moms going to be pissed.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||10-01-2001||03:13 PM||||Not an easy thing to deal with, and not having complete documentation doesn't help either.  What I would do is go done there in person first and try to reason with this guy one more time.  If he is not willing to do anything warn him that you will procede thru legal chanels.  Since he had the car 3 times and never fixed it, it would certainly indicate its his problem.<P>Do you have receipts for the work he did do on it for those other 3 times?  Also, do they show the milage of the car?  That would certainly help the case a lot.  Also, does your warrenty say anything about it being voided if you work on the car yourself?  The wording of the warrenty will come into play on this.<P>Finally find out who handles motor vehicle repair complaints.  I know in New York the DMV has a department that handles this stuff, but it might go thru the attorney generals office in other states.  Find out!  They will want to see receipts, but here in NY, they will also look at the car themselves and investigate the situation.  Just try to be honest with them, and get as much documentation as you can!  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||thomas_l||10-01-2001||03:58 PM||||Sounds like it's time to cut your losses and get the junkyard tranny the cable came from.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||10-01-2001||04:41 PM||||I already bought a a4ld trans from ebay for 60 bucks about 3 months ago.   Just in case my trans would go out after the warranty ended.<P>I have installed a trans with the help of my friend.<P>If you want to hear this story.<P>I blew a seal, doing a brake torque and the trans wasn't that great also.  NOTE the last time i did a brake torque was 3 years ago, and thats when i just bought my tbird.<P>So my friend, (he's in his 40s, takes shop class, has rebuilt trans and goes to indy, big time race fan), and I drop the trans, and brought it to the place for them to rebuild.  Its 300 bucks cheaper, i get it back.  My friend helps me put it back in, and i finish the rest when he has no time to help me with the other things.  LIke the driveshaft, coolant lines, exhaust etc.. little things.  <P>So i add the fluid in, etc... I put the car in drive and it has a hard time moving foward.  Yes the fluid level is correct.  I put more fluid in.  No effect.  As i recall, only 1 and 2 would work and D not OD.  I brought it back, and let them take it out of the car, because it was nearing Xmas, too cold outside for me to work on.   <P>I find out the OD drum is bad and another OD part.  <P>About 6months but close to a year. Or this might be the 2nd time i had it rebuild, i cant recall. I would drive my car, and when i slowed down, the whole car would shake, im thinking sh9t  my rearend is locking up.  I brought it in, and a little piece of debry is stock in the valve body.  <P>The last rebuild, i remember well, this was end of january of 2000.  Im driving my car and its slipping a tad.  I speed up to pass another car, and BAM Im in neutral.  Im lucky enough to coast it to a side street.  I call the trans shop, they got me a tow truck, which i had to pay for.  Out of warranty i guess.   <P>My mom and i waited for the truck, she was pissed.  Wonder if its cause she put more then 1600 into my car.  Took forever for the tow truck to come, not the tow company's fault really.  (note, one of the drums cracked)<P>Since i got it rebuilt.  I had problems when the trans was cold.  It didn't really wanna shift into 2nd.  And later the reverse wasn't working when i got to school and thats when the trans would be warmed up.<P>So i brought it in just like the post above.<BR>yada yada tv cable,   and i guess its related to why reverse doesn't work.<P>More likely, because its valvebody, or reverse piston is stuck.  I would believe the clutch is bad now.  <P>I looked in my chiltons, and YES i did install my tv cable correctly.  Open it full throttle and pull the cable for the linkage to be fully open on the trans and lock it up.<P>Thats BS, i dont know crap about cars.  Ive diagnosed cars better then some mechanics.  And done more then oil changes, which i hate.<BR>Install trans, change sensors, ign modules, set timing, oil pans, trans oil change on a friends car, door locks, starters, alts, rear axle bearings, brakes.  Everything except rebuilding an engine or trans.<P>What can the better business buero do for me?<BR>I cant remember what they do since consumer eco.<BR>I'm going to look for those sites on the web that you get to complain about businesses that suck.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||thomas_l||10-01-2001||06:54 PM||||Looks like you already figured it out. If you're gonna go cheap, just roll the dice on a used tranny. <P>If you want someone to build it, get them to do it start to end including R/I. That way, you haven't touched it and there's no doubt (except abuse) that you did anything to speed it's failure. With that, all you can do is cut your losses and sue if the shop won't do things right. The only hope would be if you paid with a credit card you might try getting the bank to smack em with a chargeback.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierospeeder||10-01-2001||09:26 PM||||I went to the BBB.org website aka better business (sp) beauro<P>They do have a complaint from this trans shop.  But it is from an old location they were at.  <P>Im going to call them tomorrow, or today if they are open.  <P>This is good news in a way.<BR>I'll keep you posted.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||10-02-2001||09:39 AM||||take all the paperwork you have, pay $25 and file a suit against them in small claims court. Have all papers and any witnesses with you at court.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierospeeder||11-21-2001||12:23 AM||||NEWS FLASH<P>So i got my car back today.  <P>What happened was...   My mom and i went there and we talked to the guy.  He said sorry the trans is total, it had to be rebuilt and i cant keep a warranty same with any other business that has the item been tampered with......  So my mom says  ya kids will be kids, and my son didn't drive the car for a few months etc.... <P>The guy says, well i can work with you and see what i can do.  My mom says okay.  I mentioned how i picked up a spare trans from ebay.  He says bring it in and ill use the parts from the one and build one out of two.<P><BR>It did take him a while to do my car, one- he had a lot of cars to work on ,and 2nd he had a lift go out on him so it slowed him down.<P>I got a call yesterday, and i came today with my mom to pick up my car.   He charged us NOTHING.  He did it for free, but isn't going to give us a warranty.  Eventhough the original warranty was going to expire in feb.  Thats only a few months away.<P>I asked if i can have the old trans back.  It was all apart.  But he showed me all the things that were broke.   I know the case was from my car, and i think the hardparts were from the trans i got from ebay.  The hardparts had a lot of wear in it.  I lot of scratches and some of the bearings were popped out with the springs.  So i let him keep it.<P>We talked about how bad the a4ld trans were made.  Which is true if you go to any tbird/mustang or ranger website and the a4ld is bashed so much for breaking apart.  Ive read websites where it mentions, its recomended that everything should be replaced (hardparts)<P>I said i was going to swap a t5 in it(stick).  He says its alot of work to do it.  What he and my mom doesn't know is im going to be doing that to my fiero (auto to stick conversion)<P>We thanked the mechanic/owner and he said to let him now how its running.<P>Everything works, and reverse does too.  Its a great feeling to have reverse and overdrive.   Now i have to do my repair work.  brake job/oil change etc...||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||11-21-2001||08:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierospeeder:<BR><B> I couldn't afford the plate sticker, because of TV cable.  <P>What are my options now.  Yes my moms going to be pissed.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You know, if you drop the premium channels and stop buying the pay per view p0rn0, then cable can actually be affordable for most budgets.||||reg||1
